om/repos/binkma-v/xDit-intel/contents/README.md?ref=13424d0ee55963369d3b9805ac6e8df449bbcc45", "patch": "@@ -21,13 +21,18 @@ peaking at 8.4\u00d7.\n \n ## Repository layout\n \n-This repository is the **inference engine**: a fork of\n+The artifact is split across two repositories, and **both are required**:\n+\n+| | Repository | Contents |\n+| --- | --- | --- |\n+| Engine | [`binkma-v/xDit-intel`](https://github.com/binkma-v/xDit-intel) (this one) | the `xfuser` inference engine, model drivers, jobs |\n+| Library | [`binkma-v/sp-aurora`](https://github.com/binkma-v/sp-aurora) | TAPA, V-First and V-Major themselves |\n+\n+This repository is a fork of\n [xDiT](https://github.com/xdit-project/xDiT) whose `xfuser` package is extended\n to drive the four evaluated models through CoCoDiff. The upstream project's\n README is preserved as [`README_xDiT_upstream.md`](README_xDiT_upstream.md).\n-\n-The communication mechanisms themselves live in the companion repository,\n-**sp_aurora**, which this package imports at run time. Both are required.\n+`sp_aurora` is imported at run time, not vendored.\n \n ```\n xfuser/            the engine; CoCoDiff hooks live in\n@@ -41,9 +46,13 @@ tools/plots/       figure-generating scripts\n \n ## Setup\n \n-Requires an Aurora allocation. Build and install `sp_aurora` first, then:\n+Requires an Aurora allocation. Build and install\n+[`sp-aurora`](https://github.com/binkma-v/sp-aurora) first, then:\n \n ```bash\n+git clone https://github.com/binkma-v/xDit-intel.git xDiT\n+cd xDiT\n+\n module use /soft/modulefiles/\n module load frameworks/2025.3.1\n module load oneapi/release/2025.3.1"}]}